title: The Right is expelling us from their government!
subtitle: We have angered our coalition partners too much...
new-page: true
on-arrival: tried_supporting_collectivist = 0; unionist_relation -= 6; gold_relation -= 6; ddp_relation -= 6; lvp_relation -= 6; lvp_right += 3; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 3
view-if: chancellor_party != "Marcher" and chancellor_party != "Collectivist" and marcher_in_government = 1 and ((in_grand_coalition = 1 or in_popular_front = 1 or in_minority_government = 1) and coalition_dissent >= 3) or (in_weimar_coalition = 1 and coalition_dissent >= 4) and marcher_r < 50
tags: event
go-to: menu if chancellor != "Werth"; wirth_resign_hindenburg if chancellor == "Werth" and president_ideology != "Left"; wirth_resign_braun if chancellor == "Werth" and president_ideology == "Left"

= Cabinet Reshuffled

@menu

Chancellor [+ chancellor +] has announced his intentions to President [+ president +] to reshuffle the cabinet, sacking and replacing all current <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> ministers and replacing them with bourgeois ones. [? if bourgeois_coalition < 50 and (right_coalition < 50 or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_westarp) and (center_right_coalition < 50 or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical") : Luckily, they lack a majority without us, so we can bring them down with a simple motion of no confidence. ?]

- @try_assuage: Try to assuage our partners.
- @right_coalition: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> replaces us in government.
- @center_right_coalition: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> replaces us in government.
- @minority_bruning: Askew's cabinet survives as a minority government.
- @breitscheid_vonc: Call a constructive motion of no confidence with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>!
- @sack_bruning: President [+ president +] will call snap elections.
- @bourgeois_coalition: The bourgeois have a lone majority.
- @bruning_chain: What's next?
- @tolerate: Let the reshuffle happen, and tolerate the new minority government.
- @no_tolerate: Bring down this new backstabbing government!

@try_assuage

How do we assuage our partners?

- @dvp_prussia_2: Let the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> into Heartland.
- @give_up_prussia: Give up on leadership of Heartland.
- @austerity: Enact a massive austerity plan.
- @resources: Use our resources to reduce dissent within the coalition.
- @menu: Never mind. What are our options?

@dvp_prussia_2
view-if: year <= 1929 and in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0 and (in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland) and in_grand_coalition = 1 and gold_was_in_heartland == 0 and not lvp_formed
choose-if: unionist_leader != "Renck"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unionist_leader = "Renck": Renck and the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] strongly dissents against. ?]
on-arrival: in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; gold_relation += 10; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation += 3; coalition_dissent -= 1; left_dissent += 5; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1; gold_left += 3; burgher_gold += 3

Letting the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> into the Heartland government is an offer too good for them to refuse, no matter their leadership. 

However, this has negatively impacted our freedom of action we previously had in the Unity coalition.

@give_up_prussia
subtitle: Bristol would need to resign.
view-if: heartland_leader = "Bristol" and neo_weimar_coalition_heartland >= 50
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 1; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; reformist_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; left_dissent += 5; commons_marcher -= 5; burgher_marcher -= 5; landed_marcher -= 3; braun_resign = 1

Fine. We no longer control the government of Heartland. The vote has been called off.

The Minister-President position is transferred to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

@austerity
view-if: welfare >= 0
on-arrival: coalition_dissent = 0; commons_marcher -= 10; disfavored_marcher -= 10; commons_collectivist += 7; commons_royalist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent += 5; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; disfavored += 3; collectivist_coalition_dissent += 1; collectivist_relation -= 10 if in_popular_front; goal_marcher_cancel += 1

Fine. We enacted a massive austerity program to cut welfare, in order to maintain the stability of our coalition. The vote has been called off.

@resources
choose-if: (resources >= 3 and in_weimar_coalition or in_popular_front or in_minority_government) or ((resources >= 3 and in_grand_coalition and not (gold_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and not lvp_formed) or (resources >= 3 and (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and not (lvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and lvp_formed))
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 3: We do not have enough resources. ?] [? if in_grand_coalition and (gold_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> doesn't want our resources anymore. ?] [? if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and (lvp_ideology == "Right" and year >= 1930) and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> doesn't want our resources anymore. ?]
subtitle: -3 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1

By transferring resources to our coalition partners, we can reduce their dissent against our policies. This is a crude, but effective solution.

@right_coalition
view-if: right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50
choose-if: (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)
on-arrival: center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> isn't willing to enter government.
go-to: election_1928.right_coalition_2

@center_right_coalition
view-if: right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"
choose-if: not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)
on-arrival: center_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> isn't willing to enter government.
go-to: election_1928.center_right_coalition_2

@bourgeois_coalition
view-if: bourgeois_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0
go-to: election_1928.bourgeois_coalition

@minority_bruning
view-if: constructive_vonc and not (right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and not (right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7))
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; minority_government = 1; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; lvp_right += 3; ddp_right += 3; ddp_cohesion -= 1; gold_right += 3

Due to our own constitutional reforms, we cannot bring Askew down. We will have to prepare for the next election to get our chance.

@breitscheid_vonc
view-if: constructive_vonc and not (right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and not (right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and (left_coalition >= 50 or collectivist_relation >= 50)
choose-if: left_coalition >= 50 and collectivist_relation >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_coalition < 50 : We do not have a majority in favor of Yardley. ?][? if collectivist_relation < 50 : The Communists are unwilling. ?]
on-arrival: in_left_front = 1; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; chancellor = "Yardley"; coup_progress += 3; capital_strike_progress += 2; coup_progress += 1 if in_left_front_heartland; capital_strike_progress += 1 if in_left_front_heartland; labor_minister_party = "Marcher"; interior_minister_party = "Marcher"; finance_minister_party = "Marcher"; economic_minister_party = "Marcher"; justice_minister_party = "Marcher"; foreign_minister_party = "Marcher"; agriculture_minister_party = "Marcher"; army_minister_party = "Marcher"; collectivist_relation += 10; unionist_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 10; lvp_relation -= 8; army_loyalty -= 0.05; gold_right += 10; ddp_right += 5; ddp_cohesion -= 3; lvp_right += 8; liberal_cooperation += 5; bourgeois_cooperation += 10; liberal_cooperation += 3 if in_left_front_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland; bourgeois_cooperation += 5 if in_left_front_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland; reformist_dissent += 20; reformist_strength -= 10; left_dissent -= 30; left_strength += 20

We have successfully passed a motion of no confidence to replace Askew with Yardley. We are now ruling in a united front with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

Whatever their reasoning is, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> has control over the ministries of government.

@sack_bruning
view-if: constructive_vonc and president_ideology == "Left"
choose-if: presidential_powers != 1
unavailable-subtitle: We don't have that power anymore. You really screwed us here with your reforms, you know that?
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_marcher -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; commons_marcher -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; guild_royalist += 4 if pro_republic < 50; burgher_royalist += 3 if pro_republic < 50; lvp_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; gold_right += 3

We have sacked Askew and called for new elections for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@bruning_chain
view-if: not constructive_vonc and not (right_coalition >= 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and not ((center_right_coalition >= 50 and right_coalition < 50) and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and (not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930)
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; minority_government = 1; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; bruning_event_timer = 6 if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930

Replacing us is Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], who has reorganized his cabinet to encompass the bourgeois parties. [? if not bruning_event_seen and year >= 1930: New elections haven't been called yet but it's likely that they will be soon, considering Askew most likely doesn't have the majority of the Assembly behind him. ?]

@tolerate
view-if: not constructive_vonc and (bruning_event_seen or year < 1930)
choose-if: not (right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and not (right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7))
unavailable-subtitle: They don't need us.
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; coalition_dissent = 0; left_dissent += 15; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; commons_marcher -= 3; commons_collectivist += 3; commons_royalist += 3; lvp_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; gold_left += 1
go-to: election_1928.toleration_bruning

Many in the party are incredulous. We have just been expelled from government, and our reaction is to allow this government to govern?

@no_tolerate
view-if: not constructive_vonc and (bruning_event_seen or year < 1930)
choose-if: not (right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and (traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" or traditionalist_westarp) and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7)) and not (right_coalition < 50 and center_right_coalition >= 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" and not (year = 1929 and month >= 7))
unavailable-subtitle: They don't need us.
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; foreign_minister_party = "Gold"; foreign_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; interior_minister_party = "Unionist"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Unionist"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; economic_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; finance_minister_party = "Gold"; finance_minister_party = "LVP" if lvp_formed; agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist"; labor_minister = "Sedgewick"; interior_minister = "Werth"; finance_minister = "Moldenhauer"; economic_minister = "Curtius"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser"; foreign_minister = "Stratton" if not stresemann_dead; foreign_minister = "Curtius" if stresemann_dead; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich"; army_minister = "Ravabelle"; coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 4; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; commons_marcher -= 3 if pro_republic < 50; commons_marcher -= 4 if pro_republic < 40; guild_royalist += 4 if pro_republic < 50; burgher_royalist += 3 if pro_republic < 50; welfare -= 2

The vote succeeds, and their government has resigned. Chancellor Askew remains as the head of an acting government, consisting solely of the bourgeois parties. He immediately proceeds to cut welfare spending substantially.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@wirth_resign_braun
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; chancellor = "Vesh"; chancellor_party = "Marcher"; marcher_caretaker = 1; grand_coalition_collapsed = 1 if in_grand_coalition; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; in_popular_front = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; foreign_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "I"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; army_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "I"; finance_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "I"; coalition_dissent = 0; pro_republic -= 5

Unable to bear the stress of keeping the coalition together, Werth has announced his intentions to resign as chancellor.

[+ president +] has appointed as replacement Vesh, who is immediately faced with a successful motion of no confidence. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@wirth_resign_hindenburg
on-arrival: chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"

Unable to bear the stress of keeping the coalition together, Werth has announced his intentions to resign as chancellor.

[+ president +] appoints Askew from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] as replacement, who immediately reforms the government.

- @menu: Askew sacks our ministers.
